Rules:

* Use Server Components by default.
* Add "use client" only when interactivity is required.
* Never import server-only modules into client components.
* Add import "server-only" in server-only files.
* Do not put business logic directly inside page.tsx.
* Do not write raw Prisma queries directly inside UI components.
* Use repositories/actions/services for domain logic.
* No giant files.
* No duplicated logic.
* No TypeScript any.
* No unsafe casts.
* No hardcoded services, fees, FAQs, social links, document requirements, form fields, legal content, payment instructions, or SEO metadata.
* Public pages must read dynamic data from the database.
* Admin must be able to create, update, delete, enable, disable, reorder, and SEO-optimize dynamic content.

## URL and Language Rules

PakExcise is English-only and must use clean URLs without locale prefixes.

Do not use:

* /en
* /ur
* /en/services
* /ur/services
* /en/services/[serviceSlug]
* /ur/services/[serviceSlug]

Use only clean URLs:

* /
* /services
* /services/[serviceSlug]
* /regions/[regionSlug]
* /guides/[slug]
* /blog/[slug]
* /faqs
* /track
* /about
* /contact
* /privacy
* /terms
* /disclaimer
* /refund
* /customer/dashboard
* /agent/dashboard
* /admin/dashboard

Language behavior:

* English is the only supported language.
* Do not add a language switcher.
* Do not add Urdu UI, RTL layout, or locale-prefixed routes.
* Do not redirect `/` to `/en`.
* Redirect legacy `/en/...` and `/ur/...` to the clean path with 308.
* Use next-intl with English message catalogs only and `localePrefix: "never"`.
* Navigation links, sitemap URLs, and canonical URLs must never include `/en` or `/ur`.
* Keep `<html lang="en" dir="ltr">`.
* All user-facing static strings must come from next-intl `en.json` or English DB fields.
* No hardcoded user-facing strings in components.

## i18n Content Rules

English only.

Use:

* en.json for English UI strings
* English fields in the database for admin-managed content (legacy `*Ur` columns may remain unused)

Rules:

* All user-facing static text must use next-intl English catalogs.
* All dynamic content must use English DB fields (`pickLocalized` prefers English).
* Never break page rendering because a translation is missing.
* Keep layout mobile-first LTR.
* Do not reintroduce Urdu admin fields, Noto Nastaliq, or RTL styles.

## Business Rules

PakExcise services include:

* Vehicle Transfer Punjab
* Vehicle Transfer Islamabad ICT
* Token Tax All Provinces
* New Vehicle Registration Punjab
* New Vehicle Registration Islamabad ICT
* Vehicle Inspection Punjab
* Vehicle Inspection Islamabad ICT
* Vehicle Passing / Fitness Islamabad ICT
* Route Permit Punjab
* Route Permit Islamabad ICT
* Data Correction Punjab + ICT
* Driving License Renewal Punjab + ICT
* Learner License Punjab + ICT

But do not hardcode them as permanent UI data.
Create seed data only.
Admin must manage services dynamically.

## Service Fee Rules

Never show service fees on public frontend pages.
Never show estimated service fees on service pages.
Never show pricing cards.
Fees are admin-only.
Admin sets service fee per application through invoice generator.
Invoice is the only customer-facing fee document.
Government taxes/official fees must be separated from PakExcise facilitation service fee.

## SEO Rules

Every public page must be SEO optimized.

Admin must manage:

* Meta title
* Meta description
* H1
* Canonical URL
* OG title
* OG description
* OG image
* Twitter cards
* Robots setting
* FAQ schema data
* Service schema data
* Breadcrumb schema data
* Page content
* English metadata/content fields

Use generateMetadata() on public pages.
Use server-rendered public pages.
Use dynamic sitemap.ts.
Use dynamic robots.ts.

Block private areas:

* /admin
* /customer
* /agent
* /api

Use human-readable URLs:

* /
* /services
* /services/[serviceSlug]
* /regions/[regionSlug]
* /guides/[slug]
* /faqs
* /track
* /about
* /contact
* /privacy
* /terms
* /disclaimer
* /refund
* /blog/[slug]

Use JSON-LD:

* Organization
* LocalBusiness
* Service
* FAQPage
* BreadcrumbList
* WebSite

SEO URL rules:

* Do not create `/en` URLs.
* Do not create `/ur` URLs.
* Do not include `/en` or `/ur` in sitemap.
* Do not include `/en` or `/ur` in canonical URLs.
* Do not generate duplicate language URLs.
* Clean URL is the canonical URL.
* Public pages must still be server-rendered and SEO optimized.
* Admin should manage SEO content in English; the canonical URL remains the clean path.

## UI/UX Rules

Design must be:

* Mobile-first
* Responsive for all devices
* Fast on Pakistani mobile networks
* Clean, modern, trustworthy
* Conversion-focused
* Accessible
* LTR English layout
* Dark/light/system theme compatible

Use PakExcise brand style:

* Primary: #2159BA
* Secondary: #FAC515
* Use clean white/light backgrounds and strong contrast
* Dark mode must be polished
* Avoid heavy animations
* Avoid autoplay videos
* Avoid large sliders
* Use sticky mobile CTA where useful
* WhatsApp CTA must be visible on conversion pages
* No layout shift
* Use next/image
* Provide fixed image dimensions
* Use skeletons/loading states
* Use error states
* Use empty states

## Auth & RBAC Rules

Roles:

* Guest
* Customer
* Agent
* Support Staff
* Admin
* Super Admin

Guest can:

* Browse public pages
* View services
* View FAQs
* Use contact
* Switch language/theme

Guest cannot:

* Submit application
* Upload documents
* View invoice
* View pricing

Customer can:

* Submit application
* Upload documents
* Track own applications
* View own invoice
* Upload payment screenshot
* Download own completion proof

Customer cannot:

* View other customers data
* Set fees
* Access admin

Agent can:

* Submit applications for customers
* Track assigned applications
* View commissions

Agent cannot:

* Access admin
* Set fees
* Verify payments

Support Staff can:

* View applications
* Add notes
* Contact customer
* View documents

Support Staff cannot:

* Verify payments
* Manage services
* Change critical settings

Admin can:

* Manage applications
* Manage services
* Manage FAQs
* Manage social links
* Generate invoices
* Manage status
* Verify payments
* Upload proof documents

Admin cannot:

* Delete audit logs
* Change super admin role

Super Admin can:

* Full access
* Manage users/roles
* Manage settings
* Manage feature flags
* Manage backups

Enforce RBAC on server side only.
Client-side checks are only for UX.

Every route/action must verify:

* Logged-in user
* Role permission
* Resource ownership
* Current application status
* Allowed transition

## Security Rules

Security is server-enforced.

Use:

* Zod validation on every server action, route handler, upload, and webhook
* AES-256-GCM encryption for CNIC and sensitive form fields
* bcrypt cost 12+ for passwords
* Hashed OTP
* OTP expiry 5 minutes
* OTP resend max 3 per hour
* HTTP-only secure cookies
* SameSite Strict
* CSRF protection on state-changing operations
* Upstash Redis rate limiting
* Cloudflare Turnstile on public forms
* HMAC verification for webhooks
* Signed R2 URLs only
* Virus/MIME validation for uploads
* Max file size validation
* Audit logs for all admin actions
* Append-only status history

Never:

* Store CNIC in plain text
* Store OTP in plain text
* Store passwords in plain text
* Expose private R2 URLs
* Trust client-side validation
* Send PII to analytics/pixels
* Log sensitive PII
* Commit .env files
* Expose stack traces to users
* Use unsafe raw SQL

## Application Flow Rules

Application statuses:

* SUBMITTED
* REVIEW
* DOCS_REQUIRED
* INVOICE_SENT
* PAYMENT_UPLOADED
* PAYMENT_VERIFIED
* IN_PROGRESS
* AT_OFFICE
* COMPLETED
* REJECTED
* CANCELLED

Rules:

* Every status change requires a note.
* No silent status transition.
* COMPLETED requires proof upload when service.requiresProof is true.
* Admin cannot mark COMPLETED without proof.
* Customer can only upload payment screenshot after invoice is sent.
* Admin can approve/reject payment screenshot with reason.
* Customer receives tracking ID after submission.
* Documents are uploaded to private R2 using pre-signed URLs.
* Document signed viewer URL expires in 1 hour.
* Proof download URL expires in 24 hours.

## Database Rules

Use Prisma schema with normalized tables.

Important models:

* User
* Account
* Session
* AgentProfile
* Region
* Service
* ServiceFormField
* DocumentRequirement
* Application
* ApplicationFieldValue
* Document
* Invoice
* InvoiceLineItem
* Payment
* StatusHistory
* Notification
* AuditLog
* AnalyticsAttribution
* FAQ
* SocialLink
* Setting
* SeoMeta
* Redirect
* BlogPost
* Guide

Add indexes for:

* applications(status, createdAt)
* applications(trackingId)
* applications(userId, createdAt)
* applications(agentId, createdAt)
* documents(applicationId, type)
* invoices(applicationId, status)
* payments(applicationId, status)
* services(slug)
* regions(slug)
* faqs(active, displayOrder)
* social_links(active, displayOrder)
* audit_logs(actorId, createdAt)
* analytics_attribution(source, campaign)

Use soft delete where suitable.
Audit logs must be append-only.
Changing a service slug must create a 301 redirect.

## Upload Rules

Use Cloudflare R2 private bucket.
Use pre-signed upload URLs.

Validate:

* File type
* MIME type
* Extension
* File size
* Double extension
* Virus scanning hook/queue

Allowed default formats:

* image/jpeg
* image/png
* image/webp
* application/pdf

Do not expose object keys to unauthorized users.
Use checksum where possible.

## Analytics Rules

Track:

* view_service
* click_whatsapp
* start_application
* complete_step
* upload_document
* submit_application
* invoice_viewed
* payment_uploaded
* application_completed
* click_social_link

Store attribution on every lead/application:

* first_touch_source
* first_touch_medium
* first_touch_campaign
* last_touch_source
* last_touch_campaign
* gclid
* fbclid
* ttclid
* landing_page
* referrer
* device_type

Never send:

* CNIC
* Phone number
* Email
* Full address
* Document names
* R2 keys
* Application private notes

Use event_id for deduplication with server-side events.

## Performance Rules

Targets:

* LCP under 2.5s
* CLS under 0.1
* INP under 200ms
* Cached TTFB under 300ms
* First load JS under 80KB gzipped where possible

Use:

* Server Components
* ISR for public service/region pages
* Dynamic rendering only where needed
* next/image
* WebP/AVIF
* Lazy loading
* Suspense
* loading.tsx
* error.tsx
* Pagination
* Search indexes
* Avoid N+1 queries
* Avoid heavy client bundles
* Defer third-party scripts until consent or interaction where possible

Never cache:

* Dashboards
* Signed URLs
* Private application data
* Admin pages

## Admin Dashboard Rules

Admin must manage:

* Services
* Regions
* Dynamic form fields
* Document checklists
* FAQs
* SEO
* Social links
* Applications
* Status transitions
* Invoices
* Payments
* Proof uploads
* Customers
* Agents
* Notifications
* Settings
* Audit logs
* Redirects
* Blog/guides
* English content fields

Every admin CRUD must have:

* Search
* Pagination
* Filters
* Active/inactive toggle where useful
* Display order where useful
* Validation
* Audit logging
* Confirm delete modal
* Empty state
* Loading state
* Error state

## Testing Rules

Add tests for:

* RBAC
* IDOR protection
* Status transitions
* Invoice generation
* Payment screenshot flow
* Upload validation
* Signed URL expiry
* SEO metadata generation
* Sitemap/robots
* FAQ JSON-LD
* Tracking events
* Admin CRUD actions
* English-only UI (no language switcher)
* SEO metadata generation

Before saying a feature is complete:

* Run typecheck
* Run lint
* Run tests
* Ensure no TypeScript any
* Ensure no hardcoded business data
* Ensure no frontend service fees
* Ensure no `/en` routes
* Ensure no `/ur` routes
* Ensure English-only (no language switcher / no RTL)
* Ensure mobile responsive UI
* Ensure dark mode works
* Ensure SEO metadata exists
